# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# The old WordPress slugs must 301 to the new URLs, otherwise every existing
# bookmark, email signature, business card QR code and directory listing that
# points at the old site lands on a 404. 301 (permanent) is deliberate — it is
# what passes link signals to the new URL.
#
# Apache equivalent lives in .htaccess. IIS/nginx users: see README.md.

/who              /who-we-are/     301!
/who/             /who-we-are/     301!
/triage           /nurse-triage/   301!
/triage/          /nurse-triage/   301!
/careers          /careers/        301
/contact          /contact/        301

# WordPress leftovers — no reason to serve or crawl these on a static site.
/wp-admin/*       /                301
/wp-login.php     /                301
/xmlrpc.php       /                301
/feed             /                301
/feed/            /                301
/comments/feed/   /                301

# Everything unmatched renders the styled 404 page.
/*                /404.html        404
